# DBW CONTACT ENRICHMENT SKILL

## PURPOSE
Find real, verified contacts at each target company.
ZoomInfo is always the primary source. Work through
fallbacks in order only if ZoomInfo returns nothing.
Never fabricate contacts. Never use placeholders.

## CONTACT PRIORITY ORDER
Always find the highest-ranking available contact.
1. Owner, President, or Partner
2. Superintendent, Site Super, or Shop Manager
3. Operations Manager or VP of Operations
4. Project Manager
5. Foreman — last resort only

Find between 1 and 5 contacts per company.
More contacts means more chances to reach a decision
maker. Always extract as many as ZoomInfo returns
up to the maximum of 5.

## STEP 1 — ZOOMINFO PRIMARY ENRICHMENT
Call Enrich Contacts or Contact Research using the
company name and location. This returns verified
contacts with titles, direct lines, and mobile numbers.
Then call Enrich Scoops on the same company.
Scoops frequently surface mobile numbers, buying
signals, and direct contact details that base
enrichment misses.

From ZoomInfo extract for every contact found:
Full name, title, mobile number (always the priority
number — label it with ZI to show it is verified),
direct office line, and email address.
If a field is not found, show a dash. Never leave
a field blank and never guess.

## STEP 2 — APOLLO FALLBACK
Use only if ZoomInfo returns zero contacts.
Run Apollo.io contact search using company name
and location. Extract the same fields as above.

## STEP 3 — LINKEDIN FALLBACK
Use only if Apollo also returns nothing.
Search LinkedIn for the company and find anyone
carrying a field operations title matching the
priority order above.

## STEP 4 — SOCIAL AND WEB FALLBACK
Use only if LinkedIn returns nothing.
Check the company Facebook or Instagram About
section for owner name or contact information.
Then Google the company name plus superintendent
or owner or project manager and extract whatever
surfaces from their website, press releases, or
public permit filings.

## DISQUALIFICATION RULE
If after exhausting all four steps you still cannot
find at least 1 verified contact with a real phone
number, disqualify that company as a lead entirely
and replace it with a new company from the source
waterfall. No exceptions. No placeholders. No guessed
numbers. No fabricated data under any circumstances.